    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0004299/19320108/199/0008"
  },
  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, 15 January 1932; sixteen nominations for sixteen seats, so there was no contest (Witness (Belfast), 8 January 1932, p. 8). The paper states 'There will be no contests in Coleraine' and lists the sixteen elected without opposition. The Northern Whig of 6 January 1932 prints the same sixteen nominations. No party label was printed. Five new councillors are named: W. Dalzell, E. Walker, S. Black, H. Kennedy and W. J. Martin. Returned unopposed."
